# The cheap corpus gate: 1462 edits across 42 files apply with 0 conflicts,
# //:all rebuilds clean, and a second pass has nothing left to do. Minutes, not
# the half hour abseil costs, so it is the one to run while iterating.
#
# It earned its place immediately. re2::Regexp keeps its variant fields in
# anonymous structs inside an anonymous union, with an accessor of the same
# name on the class for each -- runes_ next to Rune* runes(), hi_ next to
# int hi(). collides() consulted the field's immediate DeclContext, which is
# the anonymous struct, where nothing of that name exists; C++ looks the name
# up in the enclosing class, where the accessor does. Every one of those
# renames looked free and produced a class declaring a field and a method of
# one name -- ill-formed, and every later lookup in the class fails with it:
# 1069 errors from 7 files, all of them that. Neither googletest nor abseil
# has the shape.
#
# What it declines is almost all capture (41 of 57): re2 names a parameter
# after the member it initialises all over, so member_snake_case's dropped
# underscore lands on the parameter. That is a real hazard, not a gap.
#
# NB: this file is sourced by bash, so values must not contain backticks or the
# dollar sign.
REPO=re2
RULESET=member_snake_case
EXPECT=pass
